## Layout (macro Grid, micro Flex)

From `admin_shell` onward. **Grid** owns macro structure; **Flexbox** owns everything inside a component. Do not fight action bars (Apply + pagination, icon + label, button groups) with pure Grid alone.

### Macro (CSS Grid)

| Surface | Pattern |
| :--- | :--- |
| App shell | Sidebar + header + content area |
| Page | Vertical stack of sections (`PageChrome`, filter, content, footer) |
| Dashboard cards | `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr))` |
| Filter field matrix | Optional filter row: `grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fill,minmax(12rem,1fr))] gap-4 items-end` |

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Section owns macro template | `grid-template-columns` / `rows` on section root only |
| One chrome per region | One `PageChrome`, one filter section, one data section, one footer |
| Rhythm | `row-gap` / `column-gap` on section grid; not margin stacks between sections |

### Micro (Flexbox)

Use Flex inside components for:

| Pattern | Examples |
| :--- | :--- |
| Control internals | Icon + text, label + hint, input adornments |
| Action bars | Apply + pagination row, toolbar button groups |
| Alignment | Badge/chip content, pagination Prev/Next pair |
| Inline clusters | Filter actions cell, footer controls |

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Flex is local | Flex on toolbar, footer, action clusters, chip root — not a page-wide column replacing the section grid |
| No layout escape | No `margin-left: auto` pushing controls out of their assigned cell |
| Prefer Flex for action bars | Apply + pagination in one grid cell: inner Flex row — not a second Grid template |

Forbidden for page layout:

- Page shell or section stack as nested flex columns instead of macro Grid
- Pure Grid for action bars where Flex alignment is the natural fit
- `position: fixed` filter panels blocking content (inline accordion in flow only)
- Extra wrapper components that only add chrome (`*Chrome` around `*Chrome`)
- Hand-rolled overlay open state when a headless primitive covers the behavior (`Overlays` below)

### Section stack

`ContextBar` -> `PageChrome` -> `Toolbar` -> `[FilterPanel]` -> `Content` -> `Footer`.

### Directory filter row and pagination

Operator ask: move **Prev/Next** from list footer into the **filter grid** (bottom-right cell). That is **not** permission to relocate **Apply** or invent a second filter layout.

Canonical reference: `web/src/ui/billing/billing_filter.tsx` (Apply only); `web/src/ui/campaigns/campaigns_filter.tsx` (Apply + pagination).

#### Filter row contract

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| One filter row grid | `grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fill,minmax(12rem,1fr))]` + `items-end` (Tailwind) |
| Field cells | Each filter is a labeled field block (shadcn `Label` + control) |
| **Apply** | Direct child of filter row grid, **after** last field; shadcn `Button type="submit"`; **no wrapper** |
| **Prev/Next** | Separate direct grid child **after** Apply; `PaginationPrevNext` with `className` for column width only |
| Column width | Pagination root `w-full` of grid cell; inner **Flex** row splits Prev/Next with gap |
| Button height | Match field controls (`h-9`, `text-sm`) — not compact `text-xs` slivers |
| Footer | Remove duplicate `PaginationBar` from directory footer when pagination lives in filter row |

DOM order (campaigns-shaped directory):

```
.filterRow (grid)
  .filterField × N
  Button[Apply]
  PaginationPrevNext
```

#### Agent failure modes (forbidden)

| What agents do | Why it is wrong | Correct |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Split `filters` into `filterFields` + `filterEnd` column | Moves Apply out of the filter grid into a side column | Single `.filterRow`; all children are peers |
| Wrap Apply + pagination in `filterEndCap` / `filterActions` | Groups controls; shrinks or shifts Apply | Apply and pagination are **sibling** grid items |
| Second row (`filterRowBottom`) for Sort/Order/Apply | Breaks original row flow; operator sees Apply "moved" | Keep Sort/Order in the same `.filterRow` as other fields |
| Stack Prev/Next **above** Apply | Operator asked for horizontal pair in the grid corner, not a vertical tower | Pagination is its **own** cell beside Apply, not stacked on it |
| `margin-left: auto` on a wrapper containing Apply | Pushes Apply away from its column after Order | No auto margin on Apply; optional `justify-self` only on pagination cell if the page catalog specifies |
| Fixed `width: 5.75rem` + `justify-self: end` on pagination | Tiny buttons floating in empty grid space | `width: 100%`; fill the auto-fill column like other fields |
| Touch Apply styling/position when task is "add pagination" | Operator said pagination moves; Apply stays | Diff Apply line should be **zero** unless explicitly requested |

**Read operator layout literally:** "bottom-right corner of the filter grid" = last **grid cell** on the wrap row, not a new layout system. "Width like Apply" = width of the **grid column** Apply sits in, split 50/50 for Prev/Next — not a arbitrary `rem` constant narrower than the column.

Rejected slice: revert wrapper/column/second-row changes; restore billing-shaped Apply; add pagination as the next sibling only.

## Data tables

Admin lists are server-paginated (typically < 500 rows per page). Prefer a **semantic `<table>`** over custom CSS Grid / subgrid data matrices.

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Markup | `<table>`, `<thead>`, `<tbody>`, `<th>`, `<td>` |
| Scroll | `overflow-x-auto` wrapper; table `w-full` |
| Columns | `<colgroup>` or Tailwind column classes on `th`/`td` |
| Empty / loading | One `<tr>` with `colSpan`; or skeleton overlay — same column contract |
| Alignment | `text-align` on `th`/`td` or column class — name/money `start`, status/actions `center` |

Forbidden: bespoke subgrid row factories for standard directory tables; `display: table*` CSS pretending to be a table.

Status chips: consistent column width (`w-*` or `min-w-*` in Tailwind) so labels align across rows.

## Chips and badges

Defect class: **nested frames** (gray outer box around colored inner pill). Example failure: `.titleBadge` wrapping `FreshnessBadge`.

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| One chrome layer | Chip owns border, fill, padding; parent renders chip directly |
| Spacing | Padding from Tailwind utilities or shadcn `Badge` variants — no global padding prescription in rules |
| Vertical center | `inline-flex items-center` or shadcn `Badge` defaults inside the chip component |
| No nested frames | One `.root`; no wrapper border around semantic chip |
| Labels from API | Prefer `freshness_label`, `status_label` from handler |

## Overlays (shadcn/ui)

Complex controls are **not** built from scratch. Use **shadcn/ui** components (Radix primitives + Tailwind): `Select`, `DropdownMenu`, `Dialog`, `Popover`, `Tooltip`, `Sheet`.

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Source | Copy into `web/src/components/ui/` via shadcn CLI — do not hand-roll Radix wiring |
| Behavior from library | Focus trap, Escape, click-outside, keyboard nav, portal mount, z-index |
| Style | Tailwind on shadcn `className` slots; extend variants with `cva` inside `components/ui/` only |
| Field width | Trigger `w-full` in grid cell; content at least anchor width |
| Banned | Custom `[data-dropdown-open]` toggles, manual `document` listeners for dismiss, hand-rolled popover measure loops |

Install new primitives with `npx shadcn@latest add <component>` — keep versions aligned with `components.json`.

## Fetch and error UI

List fetch lifecycle, ticker isolation, and chart rules: `react.mdc` (Hot vs Cold).

| State | Condition | UI |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Initial load | `fetching && !data && !error` | `PageSkeleton` / grid skeleton |
| Blocking error | `error && !data` | `ErrorBlock` / `ErrorView`; no empty table |
| Stale revalidate | `data` present + error | Keep rows; toast or `AlertBanner` |
| Timeout | 15 s (`RESOURCE_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS`) | Clear `fetching` in `finally` |
| Mutation | PATCH/POST | `apiConfirmed`; toast only after 2xx |
| Empty | `items.length === 0`, filters inactive | `EmptyState` + one sentence |

No silent `catch` -> empty table. No `live: true` without `/api/v1`.

## Styling stack (Tailwind + shadcn/ui)

Markup stays **HTML via TSX**. Styling is **Tailwind utility classes** in component files. Shared controls come from **shadcn/ui** (not bespoke CSS Modules).

| Layer | Path | Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Theme | `web/src/styles/globals.css`, `tailwind.config.ts` | `@tailwind` layers; shadcn CSS variables (`--background`, `--primary`, …) |
| Primitives | `web/src/components/ui/` | shadcn copies: `Button`, `Select`, `Dialog`, `Table`, `Badge`, … |
| Utilities | `web/src/lib/utils.ts` | `cn()` — `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` |
| Domain UI | `web/src/ui/<domain>/*.tsx` | Section layout + table markup; Tailwind `className` on elements |
| Pages | `web/src/pages/*.tsx` | Compose sections only; no layout styling |

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| New work | Tailwind classes in TSX; shadcn for interactive primitives |
| `cn()` | Merge conditional classes; string args in row loops (`react.mdc`) |
| Colors | Theme tokens only (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, …) — no hard-coded hex |
| Layout | Tailwind `grid`, `flex`, `gap-*` per macro/micro rules above |
| Legacy | Existing `*.module.css` sunsets on touch — do not add new CSS Module files |

Forbidden:

- New `*.module.css` or per-domain `*.variants.ts` files
- Raw `@radix-ui/*` imports outside `components/ui/` shadcn wrappers
- Global BEM (`btn--*`, `block__element`) under `web/src/ui`
- `style={{}}` for layout (Tailwind instead)
- Pages importing stylesheets or heavy `className` trees

Gate: `bash scripts/ci/admin/ui_surface.sh`.

## Grok surfaces design system

Dark admin theme: **Grok surfaces + Geist density**. Full token table, utilities, and examples: `web/DESIGN.md`.

### Principles

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Canvas | True black (`--background`); main content breathes on `lg:p-8` |
| Depth | Surface shade steps (`ui-surface`, `ui-surface-raised`, `ui-table-frame`) — not box-shadow |
